/*****************************************************************************
    jitPJ8 -- THE PJ-8 SURVIVAL FIXTURE. 2026-08-06.

    PJ-8 rules that an action's `JiT` record is CLEARED WHEN THE ACTION IS
    COMPILED -- for jitting (jitRunAction entry) or for interpreting
    (processCode entry) -- and written at the jit capture site, with staleness
    PRECLUDED BY LIFECYCLE rather than detected by a check.

    ⚠ WHAT THIS FIXTURE EXISTS TO CATCH, and it is the one way that ruling can
    go wrong in practice. The interpreting clear is only safe because
    processCode fires ONCE per action: `field.isAction = true`
    (GroupActions.rtn:603) overwrites actionType and so consumes isCoded, while
    the call site is `if isCoded && !processCode(action)` (:549). If that
    consumption ever changes, processCode starts firing on every activation and
    THE CLEAR BEGINS ERASING RECORDS IT SHOULD KEEP -- silently, because a
    missing record looks exactly like a record that was never written.

    So the shape is jitJ1's, plus one thing: an ORDINARY INTERPRETED CALL after
    the compile, and THEN the record read back. That interpreted call is the
    hazard; if the lifetime dependency breaks, the record is gone by the time
    jitShowRecord walks the node.

    PRESENCE-WITH-VALUE (H4): jitShowRecord prints every attribute with its byte
    count, so the assertion is "JiT is there AND holds bytes", not "no error
    appeared". A deleted emitter breaks this check instead of satisfying it.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitPJ8);
define
    p8In;
    p8Out;
    jitPJ8 code={ p8Out = p8In + 5; };
    ;

p8In  = 10;
p8Out = 0;
testing(jitPJ8);
print "PJ8 fire 1: p8Out =" p8Out " (want 15)":;

p8In  = 30;
p8Out = 0;
jitRefire();
print "PJ8 fire 2: p8Out =" p8Out " (want 35, no recompile)":;

/*  ⚠ THE HAZARD ITSELF: an ordinary interpreted activation, AFTER the compile.
    If processCode re-entered here its JiT clear would wipe the record below.  */
p8In  = 10;
p8Out = 0;
jitPJ8();
print "PJ8 interpreted: p8Out =" p8Out " (the oracle -- want 15)":;

/*  THE ASSERTION. JiT must still be present and non-empty AFTER all of the
    above. Read back off the node, not off any global.  */
jitShowRecord(jitPJ8);

print "PJ8 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
